## Take the first steps

Kveikja is a partnership platform that enables us to give Icelandic companies and public bodies access to advice, testing, and training for adopting AI.

{% action href="https://www.kveikja.ai/" label="Visit website" /%}

{% cards %}
{% card title="Test new ideas" icon="kveikja-profun.svg" %}
Try out new digital technology before you invest in it. We help you assess whether a solution is feasible, what data or technology it requires, and whether the next step is testing, development, or adoption.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Help with funding" icon="kveikja-fjarmognun.svg" %}
We help you define your project more clearly, find potential partners, and identify which grants or other support might suit you.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Training" icon="kveikja-fraedsla.svg" %}
We offer training, workshops, and conversations about practical uses of AI, with a focus on the Icelandic context, the Icelandic language, and realistic adoption.
{% /card %}
{% /cards %}

## About the team

Kveikja is a partnership of five Icelandic institutions that help companies and public bodies adopt advanced digital technology.

It is part of a wider network of innovation hubs across Europe, co-funded by the European Commission to support the digital transformation of small and medium-sized enterprises and public bodies throughout Europe.

{% cards %}
{% card title="Almannarómur" logo="almannaromur" %}
Provides initial AI readiness assessments and identifies and evaluates AI use cases. Advises on language technology, with a focus on Icelandic.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Reykjavík University" logo="haskolinn-i-reykjavik.png" href="https://www.ru.is/" %}
Leads Kveikja's skills and training work. Provides training in AI and cybersecurity, along with technical support for advanced AI solutions.
{% /card %}
{% card title="University of Iceland" logo="haskoli-islands.png" href="https://hi.is/" %}
Leads Kveikja's test-before-invest work. Provides technical guidance and support for high-performance computing and AI.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Auðna Technology Transfer Office" logo="audna.png" href="https://www.audna.is/" %}
Supports Iceland's research community by protecting intellectual property and analyzing markets and the IP landscape. Leads Kveikja's communications.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Rannís (the Icelandic Centre for Research)" logo="rannis.png" %}
Coordinates Kveikja and is the main point of contact for the European Commission. Rannís also leads the work on access to funding.
{% /card %}
{% card logo="eu-co-funded.png" %}
{% /card %}
{% /cards %}
